---
description: Secret-leak prevention. Broad glob — covers config, code, IaC, CI.
globs: **/*.{tf,tfvars,yml,yaml,json,toml,ini,env,sh,py,ts,tsx,js,go,java,rs,sql,md}
alwaysApply: false
---

- NEVER commit, log, print, or hardcode: passwords, API keys, tokens, JWTs, private keys, credentials in connection strings, signed URLs, OAuth secrets, kubeconfig, real `.env` values.
- NEVER put secrets in `*.tfvars` in VCS. NEVER pass secrets as CLI positional args (visible in `ps`).
- ALWAYS reference via env vars from a secret manager (AWS/GCP/Azure, Vault, Doppler), cloud-native injection (IRSA / Workload Identity), or k8s `Secret` via CSI driver — never a literal `Secret` in VCS.
- IF a secret-shaped string is detected (`AKIA...`, `ghp_...`, `-----BEGIN ... PRIVATE KEY-----`, 32+ char high-entropy near `password=`/`token=`), STOP and ask user to rotate.
